<title>ESTONIA: INTERBANK LOAN RATES RISE SLIGHTLY.</title>
<headline>INTERBANK LOAN RATES RISE SLIGHTLY.</headline>
<dateline>TALLINN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Average interbank loan rates</p>
<p>were mostly stable with very small increases in the one-month</p>
<p>and three-month rates, the central bank said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;Most banks are seeking to borrow at present, but are not</p>
<p>too interested in longer term loans and are just looking at the</p>
<p>overnight offers,&quot; one money market trader said.</p>
<p>The weighted average rate of overnight loans for March</p>
<p>were 3.76 percent compared to February's 3.18 percent.</p>
<p> TALIBOR/TALIBID    1Week     1Month     3Months</p>
<p> April 23	   4.50/3.50  5.93/4.93  7.48/6.48</p>
<p> April 16	   4.50/3.50  5.92/4.92  7.43/6.43</p>
<p>--Tallinn newsroom +372 630 8400 reuters@reuters.ee</p>
